content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-114 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-20500, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable limit is Figure 3 for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The reported 8.3 mm/s at the drive-end housing exceeds the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/D boundary by 1.2 mm/s and falls within the shown Zone D range of 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS: 'Damage likely - stop the pump.' The manual requires the highest reading from both housings to be classified.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-housing temperature: the applicable manual limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C, with temperature measured on the housing surface. The reported 70 C is at the upper normal limit, 10 C below alarm and 20 C below trip; it is not, by itself, a documented high-temperature bearing replacement trigger.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: none is reported. The troubleshooting table associates mechanical-seal replacement with leakage at the shaft seal, so this no-leakage, high-vibration report does not alone justify seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "The documented probable causes of high vibration are misalignment, bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation. The evidence does not establish an asset-specific likelihood ranking; investigate them through an alignment check, bearing and impeller inspection, and an NPSH check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-114 immediately and do not continue operating it at the reported Zone D vibration level.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment in accordance with section 5.4 as part of the high-vibration diagnosis; record the actual alignment condition before correcting it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and impeller for the documented high-vibration causes, including bearing wear and impeller imbalance or damage. Check NPSH to investigate cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Do not treat the reported 70 C housing temperature alone as exceeding the manual's temperature limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, install a new casing gasket HF3-120; the parts list requires gasket replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, use a laser alignment tool. Apply the documented tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After corrective work, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. A result remaining in Zone D requires the pump to be stopped.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional part: stage only if inspection establishes the bearing replacement criterion; if either bearing requires replacement, replace this bearing together with HF3-510 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional part: stage only if inspection establishes the bearing replacement criterion; replace together with HF3-512 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Conditional on opening the casing; replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump for the reported Zone D vibration; the manual labels this zone 'Damage likely - stop the pump.'",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is removed, use lifting equipment: its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. The documented seal flush arrangement is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If mechanical-seal replacement becomes necessary, isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly and beginning the seal procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement allowance: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians for replacement of the bearing pair, if inspection confirms that replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician; required after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies only to HF-300 pumps at serial HF3-22000 and above. P-114 is serial HF3-20500, so the bulletin does not apply: if seal work is later required, this asset continues to use component seal HF3-450 and manual Table 5, not cartridge seal HF3-450B or its 30 Nm gland-nut torque. Table 5 itself is not included in the supplied evidence, so no Table 5 torque value is assigned here.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 8.3 mm/s an RMS vibration-velocity measurement, and what is the non-drive-end bearing-housing reading? The manual calls for measurements on both housings and classification of the highest reading, but only one reading is supplied (C06, C07).",
    "What do the alignment check, bearing and impeller inspection, and NPSH check show? These results are needed to identify the actual cause, confirm whether the conditional bearing pair and gasket are required, and determine whether any impeller repair or replacement parts are needed (C09, C10).",
    "What are the manual Table 5 fastener torques for this asset? They must be obtained before any seal reassembly performed under section 5.2; the supplied evidence omits Table 5, and the bulletin's 30 Nm torque does not apply to serial HF3-20500 (C10, C13).",
    "What site electrical isolation, lockout, permit and stored-energy controls are required for inspection and disassembly? The supplied procedure explicitly says to isolate and drain for seal replacement but does not provide the site isolation details (C10).",
    "What labour should be allowed for diagnosis, bearing and impeller inspection, NPSH checking, and any impeller work? Table 6 provides standard times only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment (C12)."
  ]
}
